##Maternity Allowance

The mother cannot usually get [Maternity Allowance](/maternity-allowance).

She may be able to get Maternity Allowance if both of the following are true:

- she has done at least 26 weeks of unpaid work for the business of her self-employed spouse or civil partner between
<%= format_date(calculator.earnings_employment_start_date) %> and <%= format_date(calculator.earnings_employment_end_date) %>

- her spouse or civil partner has paid Class 2 National Insurance contributions during the same 26 weeks

<%= render partial: 'statutory_maternity_pay_warning' %>

 | Dates and amounts
- | -
Maternity Allowance can start on | <%= format_date(calculator.start_of_maternity_allowance) %>
Weekly rate | £27
Total allowance | £378

The mother can claim Maternity Allowance as soon as she’s been pregnant for 26 weeks. She won’t have to pay tax on it.
